<title>USA: Capital Savings votes split, payout rise.</title>
<headline>Capital Savings votes split, payout rise.</headline>
<dateline>JEFFERSON CITY, Mo. 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Capital Savings Corp Inc said on Friday its board approved a two-for-one stock split in the form of a 100 percent stock dividend.</p>
<p>The board also voted a cash dividend of $0.12 per share on the pre-split shares, which represents a 33 percent increase from the $0.09 per share paid in the previous quarter.</p>
<p>The $0.12 per share dividend equates to $0.06 per share following the split.</p>
<p>Both the split and the quarterly dividend will be paid November 22, record November 8.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
